{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"insentient-aware-anole","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe MCP reference generator selects the first physical description line. Wrapped registrar prose therefore yields truncated summaries. The accepted first-line choice is recorded on `lupine-clearcut-mare`. The `transition_ticket` registrar also says close classes are ignored for non-bug tickets although the administrative subset is supported.\n\n## Plan\n- Normalize the complete first description paragraph into one generated summary.\n- Stop summary extraction at the next paragraph.\n- Correct the `transition_ticket` registrar description without changing its schema or behavior.\n- Regenerate `docs/mcp-reference.md`.\n- Add focused generator and registrar contract tests.\n- Do not add duplicate summary metadata or a general prose validator.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every generated MCP summary is a complete first paragraph rather than a physical-line fragment.\n- [ ] Wrapped descriptions render as one complete summary.\n- [ ] Paragraphs after the summary remain excluded.\n- [ ] `transition_ticket` documents bug classifications and the non-bug administrative subset accurately.\n- [ ] Generated-reference and focused MCP tests pass.\n- [ ] MCP schemas and runtime behavior are unchanged.","id":"0b58-cdd8-cfed-4a07","parent_id":"f7e4-4d33-f231-4774","priority":1,"tags":["documentation","f13","mcp"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"F13 generate complete MCP summaries"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787417237300883001,"uuid":"a2a978f0-7387-4187-a1ef-37bea18589e3"}